    {
      "id": "n_sticky_main",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1360,
        -864
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## 08-23-01 turn forwarded business documents into structured records with AI\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Forward any business document (receipt, invoice, contract, ID, bank statement, bill) as a photo or screenshot to a webhook.\n2. The workflow validates that an image arrived, then sends it to GPT-4o Vision to classify the document type and extract the key fields into a structured record.\n3. The record is stored in Postgres, then posted to a Discord channel and emailed to the operations inbox.\n4. If the image is unreadable, the team is alerted on Discord and by email so nothing is lost.\n5. A daily 8am sweep finds documents still open from the previous day or earlier and sends a follow-up reminder on Discord and by email, or an all-clear when nothing is pending.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n1. Create the Postgres table `biz_documents` (see notes in registry).\n2. Point the webhook at your capture channel (Zapier, Make, email parser, or a phone number that forwards to the URL).\n3. Set the Discord channel, the operations email, and the OpenAI credential (gpt-4o vision).\n4. Activate. Forward a test receipt and confirm it appears in Postgres, Discord, and email.\n\n### Customization\n\n- Change `doc_type` routing to push invoices to accounting and contracts to legal.\n- Add an Airtable or Sheets mirror for non-technical reporting.\n- Swap the vision model for Gemini or Claude if you prefer."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
